// The kinds of work in the inventory, written down once. Each line is one specialisation: what it is called, the titles
// that name it, the words its postings and résumés carry, and the specialisations a person in it can move to (with how
// readily, 0–1). A function groups specialisations and has its own generic titles ("Developer L3", "Analyst"), which say
// the function but not the specialisation; the text then decides.
//
// Built from the open Bengaluru inventory of 24 Nov 2026 (23,961 valid postings): the frequent titles and their words,
// read by hand. Not from résumés, and not from any labelled pair. Code only: no model reads anything here.
//
// Line format:   id | plain label | title pattern | signature words, comma separated | neighbours "id:weight ..."
// Function line: # fn | plain label | generic title pattern
// A title pattern is a case-insensitive regular expression tested on the cleaned title. "!" starts an exclusion: a title
// that matches it is never this specialisation ("tester!manager" reads "tester" but not "test manager").

